Let $k\in {\mathbb N}$ with $1\le k\le n$ and $C\in [1,\infty)$.
We say that ${\hyperref[induct positive terms]{{\rm InductPositiveTerms}(k,C)}}$ holds if

for all $\gamma=(k,u,a)\in \Gamma$, $i\in [k)$,
\begin{equation}
\|\mathbf{M}(\gamma,s_{\gamma} \otimes s_{\gamma},i)\|_{{\rm M}(k)}\le C \Delta_\gamma^{2-2^{k-n+1}}.
\end{equation}

Let $k\in {\mathbb N}$ with $1\le k\le n$ and $C\in [1,\infty)$.
We say that ${\hyperref[vanishing diagonal]{{\rm VanishingDiagonal}(k,C)}}$ holds if

for all $\gamma=(k,u,a)\in \Gamma$, $i\in [k)$,
